{
  "mn81:0.1": "Middle Discourses 81 ",
  "mn81:0.2": "With Ghaṭīkāra ",
  "mn81:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "mn81:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was wandering in the land of the Kosalans together with a large Saṅgha of mendicants. ",
  "mn81:2.1": "Then the Buddha left the road, and at a certain spot he smiled. ",
  "mn81:2.2": "Then Venerable Ānanda thought, ",
  "mn81:2.3": "“What is the cause, what is the reason why the Buddha smiled? ",
  "mn81:2.4": "Realized Ones do not smile for no reason.” ",
  "mn81:2.5": "So Ānanda arranged his robe over one shoulder, raised his cupped palms toward the Buddha, and said, ",
  "mn81:2.6": "“What is the cause, what is the reason why the Buddha smiled? ",
  "mn81:2.7": "Realized Ones do not smile for no reason.” ",
  "mn81:3.1": "“Once upon a time, Ānanda, there was a market town in this spot named Vebhaliṅga. It was successful and prosperous, populous and full of people. ",
  "mn81:3.2": "And Kassapa, a blessed one, a perfected one, a fully awakened Buddha, lived supported by Vebhaliṅga. ",
  "mn81:3.3": "It was here, in fact, that he had his monastery, ",
  "mn81:3.4": "where he advised the mendicant Saṅgha while seated.” ",
  "mn81:4.1": "Then Ānanda spread out his outer robe folded in four and said to the Buddha, ",
  "mn81:4.2": "“Well then, sir, may the Blessed One sit here! ",
  "mn81:4.3": "Then this piece of land will have been occupied by two perfected ones, fully awakened Buddhas.” ",
  "mn81:4.4": "The Buddha sat down on the s